      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings are valid when a system consumes everything it touches, but choosing to stop playing the game doesn't mean you have to destroy yourself; it simply means reclaiming your life from the moment you cross the threshold of that workplace. This struggle often leads to burnout because we are taught to believe that our value lies entirely in our productivity within a corporate machine. However, refusing to perform within that system is a powerful act of resistance that allows your soul to breathe again, not by winning the game, but by opting out of its rules entirely.",
      "source": "target",
